1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,911
This country sits 2 meters above
the sea, and the sea keeps rising.

2
00:00:04,391 --> 00:00:08,017
This is Tuvalu, a name that
means eight standing together.

3
00:00:08,447 --> 00:00:11,153
About 11,000 people
live on 9 small islands,

4
00:00:11,183 --> 00:00:13,702
and the highest point is only 4.6 meters.

5
00:00:14,132 --> 00:00:18,036
So how does a country this
small survive? It has 3 plans,

6
00:00:18,066 --> 00:00:20,176
and the first one is 2 letters.

7
00:00:20,606 --> 00:00:24,038
In 1998, Tuvalu noticed that
its internet code, dot TV,

8
00:00:24,068 --> 00:00:25,989
looks like the word television.

9
00:00:26,419 --> 00:00:27,944
It leased that domain to a company,

10
00:00:27,974 --> 00:00:30,833
and the payments became about one
twelfth of the national income.

11
00:00:31,263 --> 00:00:34,158
Every time you open Twitch,
you are typing Tuvalu's code.

12
00:00:34,588 --> 00:00:38,047
In 2021, it chose a new company,
GoDaddy, to run the domain.

13
00:00:38,477 --> 00:00:44,021
But money cannot stop water. So what is
daily life like on an island this small?

14
00:00:44,451 --> 00:00:48,761
The capital, Funafuti, has an airport
built by the United States Navy in 1943.

15
00:00:49,191 --> 00:00:51,333
Flights from Fiji land
only a few times a week,

16
00:00:51,363 --> 00:00:53,182
and there is no fence around the runway.

17
00:00:53,612 --> 00:00:57,525
So when the plane is gone, the runway
becomes the town park, with soccer,

18
00:00:57,555 --> 00:00:59,469
volleyball, and even laundry drying.

19
00:00:59,899 --> 00:01:04,217
There is simply no space. The whole
country covers about 26 square kilometers,

20
00:01:04,247 --> 00:01:07,060
and more than half of its
people live on one atoll.

21
00:01:07,490 --> 00:01:10,465
That brings us to plan 2:
a way out for the people.

22
00:01:10,895 --> 00:01:13,872
In 2023, Tuvalu signed
a treaty with Australia.

23
00:01:14,302 --> 00:01:18,783
It lets 280 Tuvaluans move to Australia
every year, chosen by lottery.

24
00:01:19,213 --> 00:01:23,666
When the lottery opened in 2025, more
than a third of the country registered.

25
00:01:23,696 --> 00:01:25,354
That is a way out for people.

26
00:01:25,784 --> 00:01:27,323
But what about the country itself?

27
00:01:27,753 --> 00:01:28,457
Back in 2021,

28
00:01:28,487 --> 00:01:32,859
Tuvalu's foreign minister gave a climate
speech standing knee-deep in the sea.

29
00:01:33,289 --> 00:01:35,533
A year later, he announced the third plan:

30
00:01:35,563 --> 00:01:37,862
copy the entire country
into the metaverse.

31
00:01:38,292 --> 00:01:40,954
The first piece is a digital
twin of one small islet,

32
00:01:40,984 --> 00:01:43,087
expected to be among the first underwater.

33
00:01:43,517 --> 00:01:46,620
The idea is that Tuvalu could
keep its land, its culture,

34
00:01:46,650 --> 00:01:50,138
and its government working, even
if the water takes the islands.

35
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:53,534
Tuvalu says it would be
the first country to do it.

36
00:01:53,964 --> 00:01:58,283
Tuvalu became independent in
1978. Less than 50 years later,

37
00:01:58,313 --> 00:02:02,197
it is planning for a world
where its islands are gone.

38
00:02:04,377 --> 00:02:08,505
That was Tuvalu. Which country should
we visit next? Tell me in the comments.

